      "writtenOn": "2024-03-05T10:08:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@elsk@google.com @umendez@google.com @sidnayyar@google.com\n\nGetting Kleaf to add the one-line `rust_defconfig` fragment containing `CONFIG_RUST` unconditionally also pulls in some more things.\n\nMore importantly it actually compiles and/or links some Rust code somewhere. I know this, because it crashes `stg`. (The fix has been ready for some time.)\n\nSo if we want an intermediate step, it is just `CONSTRUCTORS`. Otherwise, we can go `RUST`, but we need at least one more tooling piece in place first.\n\nThere are also warnings about `bindgen` being too new.",
      "parentUuid": "3b642848_33abfc3a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 123,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 123,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "a9c81b2fe524def5bc7b7e5aab71497b74727e8d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "82b78e48_ef67035e",
        "filename": "init/Kconfig",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 123,
      "author": {
        "id": 1961395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-05T14:39:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e unconditionally also pulls in some more things.\n\nDo we know which things? From Kleaf\u0027s PoV the [rust_defconfig](https://cs.android.com/android/kernel/superproject/+/common-android-mainline:build/kernel/kleaf/impl/defconfig/rust_defconfig) sets `CONFIG_RUST\u003dy` which is WAI.\n\nBy looking at ([Kconfig](https://cs.android.com/android/kernel/superproject/+/common-android-mainline:common/init/Kconfig;l\u003d1884-1904)) this has the effect of selecting `CONSTRUCTORS` (this change) but also from the [Kbuild](https://cs.android.com/android/kernel/superproject/+/common-android-mainline:common/Kbuild;l\u003d92) it pulls in the `rust/` ACK subdirectory, is this the problematic bit?",
      "parentUuid": "d96cec3e_b23bdc87",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 123,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 123,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "a9c81b2fe524def5bc7b7e5aab71497b74727e8d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cd0c4ecd_45b33957",
        "filename": "init/Kconfig",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 123,
      "author": {
        "id": 1961395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-05T15:08:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e There are also warnings about bindgen being too new.\n\nI see the warning coming from [scripts/rust_is_available.sh](https://cs.android.com/android/kernel/superproject/+/common-android-mainline:common/scripts/rust_is_available.sh;l\u003d168-175); probably invoked [here](https://cs.android.com/android/kernel/superproject/+/common-android-mainline:common/Makefile;l\u003d1255-1260)?",
      "parentUuid": "82b78e48_ef67035e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 123,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 123,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "a9c81b2fe524def5bc7b7e5aab71497b74727e8d",
